Declare tar.bzl's toolchain hub repo reproducible so it can use the repo contents cache.

Upstream marked `bsdtar_binary_repo` reproducible in
https://github.com/bazel-contrib/tar.bzl/pull/95 but stopped short of
`tar_toolchains_repo`, which only writes a generated BUILD file derived from its own
attributes and is therefore trivially reproducible. Without this, `bsd_tar_toolchains`
misses the remote repo contents cache on every CI runner.

Not yet raised upstream.

--- a/tar/toolchain/toolchain.bzl
+++ b/tar/toolchain/toolchain.bzl
@@ -131,6 +131,12 @@
 
     rctx.file("BUILD.bazel", build_content)
 
+    # Bazel <8.3.0 lacks rctx.repo_metadata
+    if not hasattr(rctx, "repo_metadata"):
+        return None
+
+    return rctx.repo_metadata(reproducible = True)
+
 tar_toolchains_repo = repository_rule(
     _tar_toolchains_repo_impl,
     doc = """Creates a repository that exposes a tar_toolchain_type target.""",
